Copied from pktmon 0.6.2 on crates.io (https://github.com/emmachase/pktmon, MIT, see LICENSE), patched in through
[patch.crates-io] in the workspace Cargo.toml. Changed, each marked "Nous Relic Importer" in the source:

- src/legacy/etw.rs: its own ETW session name and GUID (upstream: "PktMon-Consumer"). Every app on this crate
  shares upstream's, and each one's start closes the session of that name, so on Windows 10 starting Reliquary
  Archiver silenced this app and the other way round.
- src/realtime/mod.rs: its own live session name (upstream: "PktMon Rust").
- src/lib.rs: Capture::new_legacy(), the Windows 10 backend on any Windows, for testing it on Windows 11.
- src/realtime/c_api.rs: extern "system" for upstream's "stdcall", the same ABI on x64 without a warning per line.

